      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Cap d'Erquy"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Falaises de grès rose et landes sauvages. Un des plus beaux points de vue de la Côte d'Émeraude.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Pink sandstone cliffs and wild moorland. One of the finest viewpoints on the Emerald Coast."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Dahouet": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Dahouet"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Petit port discret niché dans une ria, longtemps ignoré des cartes marines pour rester secret des pêcheurs locaux.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A discreet little port tucked into a tidal inlet, long left off nautical charts to stay a local fishermen's secret."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Chemin de Stevenson": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Stevenson Trail"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Le Puy-en-Velay → La Bastide-Puylaurent — 75 km": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Le Puy-en-Velay → La Bastide-Puylaurent — 75 km"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Le Puy-en-Velay": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Le Puy-en-Velay"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Départ au pied de la statue de Notre-Dame-de-France, sur les traces de Robert Louis Stevenson et de son ânesse Modestine.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Starting point at the foot of the Notre-Dame-de-France statue, following in the footsteps of Robert Louis Stevenson and his donkey Modestine."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Bouchet-Saint-Nicolas": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Bouchet-Saint-Nicolas"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Le village où Stevenson acheta Modestine. Les premiers plateaux du Velay, à l'air déjà plus rude.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The village where Stevenson bought Modestine. The first plateaus of the Velay, the air already turning rougher."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Pradelles": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Pradelles"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Village fortifié perché sur son éperon rocheux, aux portes de la Lozère et de ses grands espaces vides.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A fortified village perched on its rocky spur, at the gates of the Lozère and its vast empty spaces."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Langogne": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Langogne"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Halte au bord de l'Allier naissant. Stevenson y écrivit ses premières impressions désabusées sur son ânesse récalcitrante.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A stop by the young river Allier. Stevenson wrote his first disillusioned impressions of his stubborn donkey here."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "La Bastide-Puylaurent": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "La Bastide-Puylaurent"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Aux portes des Cévennes, le point d'arrivée de cette première étape — le chemin continue vers l'Ardèche pour qui veut poursuivre.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "At the gates of the Cévennes, the endpoint of this first stage — the trail continues toward the Ardèche for those who wish to carry on."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "GR20 Nord": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "GR20 North"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Calenzana → Vizzavona — 90 km": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Calenzana → Vizzavona — 90 km"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Le clocher baroque du village balata marque le vrai départ du GR20 — réputé le plus difficile d'Europe.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The village's baroque bell tower marks the true start of the GR20 — reputed to be the toughest trek in Europe."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Refuge de Tighjettu": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Tighjettu Hut"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Isolé au cœur du massif, entouré de sommets acérés. Un des refuges les plus reculés de toute la traversée.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Isolated at the heart of the massif, surrounded by jagged peaks. One of the most remote huts on the whole crossing."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Refuge de Ciottulu di i Mori": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Ciottulu di i Mori Hut"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Perché à plus de 1 900 m sous le Paglia Orba, un des plus beaux promontoires de l'île pour un lever de soleil.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Perched above 1,900 m beneath the Paglia Orba, one of the island's finest spots for a sunrise."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Le village-frontière entre le nord alpin et le sud plus doux du GR20 — la moitié du chemin, à l'ombre de la forêt de pins laricio.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The border village between the alpine north and the gentler south of the GR20 — the halfway point, in the shade of the laricio pine forest."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Route Royale Perse": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Persian Royal Road"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Suse → Sardes — l'autoroute de Darius Ier": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Susa → Sardis — Darius I's highway"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Suse": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Susa"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Capitale perse, résidence d'hiver de Darius Ier. Point de départ de la route royale la plus rapide du monde antique.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Persian capital, winter residence of Darius I. Starting point of the fastest road in the ancient world."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Pasargades": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Pasargadae"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Première capitale perse fondée par Cyrus le Grand, où se dresse son tombeau. Berceau de la dynastie achéménide.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The first Persian capital, founded by Cyrus the Great, whose tomb stands here. Cradle of the Achaemenid dynasty."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Persépolis": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Persepolis"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Capitale cérémonielle achéménide, où les tributs de l'empire entier affluaient à chaque printemps.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The Achaemenid ceremonial capital, where tribute from across the empire poured in every spring."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Ecbatane": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Ecbatana"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Capitale des Mèdes, résidence d'été aux sept murailles colorées. Relais stratégique sur la route de l'ouest.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Capital of the Medes, a summer residence with seven colored walls. A strategic relay on the western road."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Mésopotamie": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Mesopotamia"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Traversée du cœur de l'empire entre Tigre et Euphrate, berceau des civilisations et grenier du monde perse.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Crossing the heart of the empire between the Tigris and Euphrates, cradle of civilizations and granary of the Persian world."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Babylone": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Babylon"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "La cité de la porte d'Ishtar et des jardins suspendus. Le cœur battant du monde antique sur l'Euphrate.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The city of the Ishtar Gate and the Hanging Gardens. The beating heart of the ancient world on the Euphrates."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Ninive": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Nineveh"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Ancienne capitale assyrienne sur le Tigre, aux palais couverts de bas-reliefs de lions et de rois chasseurs.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The former Assyrian capital on the Tigris, its palaces covered in reliefs of lions and royal hunters."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Harran": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Harran"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Cité caravanière de Haute-Mésopotamie, célèbre pour son temple lunaire. Carrefour vers l'Anatolie.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A caravan city in Upper Mesopotamia, famous for its temple to the moon god. A crossroads toward Anatolia."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Passage de l'Euphrate": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Crossing the Euphrates"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Le grand fleuve franchi sur des barques de peaux gonflées. La route bascule vers les hauts plateaux anatoliens.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The great river crossed on rafts of inflated skins. The road turns toward the Anatolian highlands."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Gordion": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Gordium"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Capitale phrygienne au nœud légendaire qu'Alexandre trancherait plus tard. Dernière grande étape avant la Lydie.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The Phrygian capital with its legendary knot, later cut by Alexander. The last major stop before Lydia."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Sardes": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Sardis"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Terminus occidental sur la mer Égée. Les cavaliers royaux couvraient ce trajet en sept jours grâce aux relais de poste.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The western terminus on the Aegean Sea. Royal couriers covered this route in seven days thanks to relay stations."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Alexandre le Grand — Campagne perse": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Alexander the Great — Persian Campaign"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Macédoine → Persépolis": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Macedon → Persepolis"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Pella": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Pella"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Capitale macédonienne où Alexandre fut éduqué par Aristote. Départ de la plus grande armée que la Grèce ait jamais vue.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The Macedonian capital where Alexander was tutored by Aristotle. Departure of the greatest army Greece had ever seen."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Bataille du Granique": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Battle of the Granicus"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Première victoire décisive contre les satrapes perses en 334 av. J.-C. Alexandre manque d'y être tué.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "First decisive victory over the Persian satraps in 334 BC. Alexander narrowly escapes death."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "La riche capitale lydienne se rend sans combat. L'Ionie grecque est libérée de la tutelle perse.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The wealthy Lydian capital surrenders without a fight. Greek Ionia is freed from Persian rule."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Halicarnasse": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Halicarnassus"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Siège de la cité carienne et de son port. La flotte perse perd sa dernière grande base en mer Égée.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Siege of the Carian city and its harbor. The Persian fleet loses its last major base in the Aegean."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Bataille d'Issos": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Battle of Issus"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Darius III en fuite, sa famille capturée. L'empire perse commence à vaciller sous les coups macédoniens.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Darius III flees, his family captured. The Persian empire begins to falter under Macedonian blows."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Siège de Tyr": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Siege of Tyre"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Sept mois de siège contre la cité phénicienne insulaire. Alexandre fait bâtir une digue jusqu'aux remparts.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Seven months besieging the island city of Phoenicia. Alexander has a causeway built to the walls."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Alexandrie d'Égypte": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Alexandria, Egypt"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Alexandre trace lui-même le plan de la ville qui portera son nom et deviendra un phare de la culture antique.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Alexander personally lays out the plan for the city that will bear his name and become a beacon of ancient culture."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Bataille de Gaugamèles": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Battle of Gaugamela"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "L'affrontement décisif contre Darius III. L'Empire perse achéménide s'effondre pour de bon en 331 av. J.-C.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The decisive clash against Darius III. The Achaemenid Persian Empire collapses for good in 331 BC."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "La plus grande ville du monde prise sans combat. Alexandre se présente en libérateur plutôt qu'en conquérant.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The greatest city in the world taken without a fight. Alexander presents himself as a liberator rather than a conqueror."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Le trésor royal perse tombe intact aux mains d'Alexandre. Des richesses inouïes changent de camp.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The Persian royal treasury falls intact into Alexander's hands. Untold riches change sides."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Portes Persiques": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Persian Gates"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Défilé montagneux défendu par les Perses, forcé de nuit par une manœuvre de contournement. Dernier verrou avant la capitale.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A mountain pass defended by the Persians, forced open at night by a flanking maneuver. The last barrier before the capital."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "La cité des rois achéménides incendiée après sa prise. La Perse est conquise, l'objectif d'Alexandre accompli.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The city of the Achaemenid kings, burned after its capture. Persia is conquered, Alexander's goal achieved."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Alexandre le Grand — Épopée complète": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Alexander the Great — The Complete Epic"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Macédoine → Inde — 8 ans de conquête": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Macedon → India — 8 years of conquest"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Capitale macédonienne, départ de la plus grande épopée militaire de l'Antiquité en 334 av. J.-C.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The Macedonian capital, starting point of the greatest military epic of antiquity in 334 BC."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Troie": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Troy"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Premier arrêt symbolique — Alexandre se recueille sur la tombe d'Achille, le héros auquel il s'identifiait.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "First symbolic stop — Alexander pays his respects at the tomb of Achilles, the hero he identified with."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Première grande victoire contre Darius III en personne. La famille royale perse tombe aux mains d'Alexandre.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "First major victory against Darius III in person. The Persian royal family falls into Alexander's hands."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Tyr et l'Égypte": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Tyre and Egypt"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Après sept mois de siège contre Tyr, Alexandre descend en Égypte et fonde Alexandrie sur le delta du Nil.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "After a seven-month siege of Tyre, Alexander moves down into Egypt and founds Alexandria on the Nile delta."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Gaugamèles": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Gaugamela"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Victoire décisive contre Darius III qui met fin à l'Empire perse achéménide en 331 av. J.-C.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A decisive victory over Darius III that ends the Achaemenid Persian Empire in 331 BC."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Capitale cérémonielle persane. L'incendie reste l'acte le plus controversé de toute la conquête.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The Persian ceremonial capital. Its burning remains the most controversial act of the entire conquest."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Poursuite de Darius, retrouvé assassiné par ses propres satrapes. Alexandre lui offre des funérailles royales.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The pursuit of Darius, found murdered by his own satraps. Alexander gives him a royal funeral."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Bactres": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Bactra"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Aux portes de l'Asie centrale, Alexandre épouse Roxane. La résistance bactriène est la plus farouche rencontrée.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "At the gates of Central Asia, Alexander marries Roxana. Bactrian resistance is the fiercest he has faced."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Sogdiane": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Sogdiana"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Deux ans de guérilla épuisante contre Spitamène dans les montagnes d'Asie centrale. La conquête la plus dure.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Two exhausting years of guerrilla warfare against Spitamenes in the mountains of Central Asia. The hardest conquest of all."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Hindū Kush": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Hindu Kush"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Franchissement des montagnes enneigées vers l'Inde. L'armée souffre du froid, de l'altitude et de la faim.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Crossing the snow-covered mountains toward India. The army suffers from cold, altitude, and hunger."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Taxila": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Taxila"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Première grande cité indienne. Le roi Poros attend sur l'Hydaspe avec deux cents éléphants de guerre.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The first great Indian city. King Porus waits on the Hydaspes with two hundred war elephants."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Bataille de l'Hydaspe": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Battle of the Hydaspes"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Victoire contre Poros et ses éléphants, sous la pluie de mousson. La bataille la plus coûteuse de la campagne.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Victory over Porus and his elephants, in the monsoon rain. The costliest battle of the campaign."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Rivière Beas": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Hyphasis River"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "La mutinerie. Les soldats refusent d'avancer vers l'Inde profonde. Alexandre pleure dans sa tente, puis accepte de rentrer.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The mutiny. The soldiers refuse to march further into India. Alexander weeps in his tent, then agrees to turn back."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Désert de Gédrosie": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Gedrosian Desert"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "La retraite cauchemardesque. Des milliers d'hommes meurent de soif dans les sables du Makran.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The nightmarish retreat. Thousands of men die of thirst in the sands of the Makran."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Noces de Suse": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Susa Weddings"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Alexandre marie ses officiers à des princesses perses pour fondre Grecs et Orientaux en un seul peuple.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Alexander marries his officers to Persian princesses to merge Greeks and easterners into a single people."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Deuil d'Héphaïstion": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Mourning Hephaestion"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "La mort de son ami le plus cher, à Ecbatane, plonge Alexandre dans un deuil dévastateur.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The death of his dearest friend, at Ecbatana, plunges Alexander into devastating grief."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Mort d'Alexandre à 32 ans, en 323 av. J.-C. Son empire, le plus vaste jamais conquis, est aussitôt démembré.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Alexander dies at 32, in 323 BC. His empire, the largest ever conquered, is dismembered almost immediately."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Route de la Soie": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Silk Road"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Chang'an → Rome — 2 000 ans de commerce": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Chang'an → Rome — 2,000 years of trade"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Xi'an": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Xi'an"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Ancienne Chang'an, capitale des Han et des Tang. Les caravanes de chameaux chargées de soie partaient d'ici vers l'ouest.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The former Chang'an, capital of the Han and Tang dynasties. Camel caravans loaded with silk set off westward from here."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Lanzhou": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Lanzhou"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Verrou du fleuve Jaune, porte du corridor du Hexi. Les caravanes s'y regroupent avant les grands déserts.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A gateway on the Yellow River, entrance to the Hexi Corridor. Caravans gathered here before the great deserts."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Jiayuguan": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Jiayuguan"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Extrémité ouest de la Grande Muraille, dernière forteresse de l'empire. Au-delà commençait l'inconnu.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The western end of the Great Wall, the empire's last fortress. Beyond it lay the unknown."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Dunhuang": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Dunhuang"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Oasis du désert de Gobi, gardienne des Grottes de Mogao aux mille bouddhas sculptés dans la roche ocre.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "An oasis in the Gobi Desert, guardian of the Mogao Caves with their thousand Buddhas carved into ochre rock."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Tourfan": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Turpan"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Oasis sous le niveau de la mer, irriguée par les canaux karez. Vignes et bouddhas au cœur de la fournaise du Taklamakan.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "An oasis below sea level, irrigated by karez canals. Vineyards and Buddhas in the heart of the Taklamakan furnace."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Kashgar": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Kashgar"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Grand carrefour au pied du Pamir, où se rejoignent les routes du nord et du sud du désert.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A major crossroads at the foot of the Pamirs, where the northern and southern desert routes meet."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Samarcande": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Samarkand"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Joyau de l'Asie centrale, carrefour de toutes les caravanes. Tamerlan en fit la capitale de son empire au XIVe siècle.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A jewel of Central Asia, crossroads of every caravan. Tamerlane made it the capital of his empire in the 14th century."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Boukhara": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Bukhara"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Ville sainte aux cent médersas, joyau spirituel et marchand de l'Asie centrale.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A holy city with a hundred madrasas, a spiritual and mercantile jewel of Central Asia."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Merv": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Merv"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Oasis géante du Turkménistan, l'une des plus grandes villes du monde médiéval avant sa destruction par les Mongols.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A giant oasis in Turkmenistan, one of the largest cities in the medieval world before its destruction by the Mongols."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "L'ancienne capitale perse ruinée par Alexandre, toujours imposante sur le passage des marchands.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The former Persian capital, ruined by Alexander, still imposing along the merchants' route."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Bagdad": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Baghdad"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Capitale abbasside et sa Maison de la Sagesse, où le savoir grec, perse et indien se traduisait en arabe.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The Abbasid capital and its House of Wisdom, where Greek, Persian, and Indian knowledge was translated into Arabic."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Constantinople": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Constantinople"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "La ville-carrefour entre Europe et Asie, où Orient et Occident échangeaient richesses et savoirs depuis des siècles.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The crossroads city between Europe and Asia, where East and West had traded riches and knowledge for centuries."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Terminus occidental. La soie chinoise habillait les sénateurs romains. Deux empires reliés sans jamais se rencontrer.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The western terminus. Chinese silk clothed Roman senators. Two empires connected, yet never meeting."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Marco Polo — Venise → Chine": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Marco Polo — Venice to China"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "24 ans de voyage à la cour de Kubilaï Khan": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "24 years of travel to the court of Kublai Khan"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Venise": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Venice"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Départ en 1271 avec son père et son oncle, marchands habitués des routes orientales.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Departure in 1271 with his father and uncle, merchants well used to the eastern trade routes."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Acre": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Acre"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Escale en Terre sainte. Les Polo y obtiennent des lettres du pape et de l'huile du Saint-Sépulcre pour le Grand Khan.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A stop in the Holy Land. The Polos obtain letters from the Pope and oil from the Holy Sepulchre for the Great Khan."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Première grande escale dans la ville-carrefour de la Méditerranée orientale, centre du commerce mondial.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The first great stopover in the crossroads city of the eastern Mediterranean, a hub of world trade."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Trébizonde": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Trebizond"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Port de la mer Noire, terminus des routes caravanières d'Anatolie orientale.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A Black Sea port, terminus of the caravan routes from eastern Anatolia."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Tabriz": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Tabriz"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Grande cité marchande de Perse, plaque tournante des perles, des soies et des épices.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A great merchant city of Persia, a hub for pearls, silks, and spices."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Ormuz": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Hormuz"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Port du Golfe Persique. Marco vit des navires si fragiles qu'il refusa d'embarquer et continua par voie terrestre.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A port on the Persian Gulf. Marco saw ships so fragile he refused to sail and continued overland instead."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Kerman": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Kerman"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Ville persane réputée pour ses turquoises et ses tapis. Les Polo renoncent à la mer pour la piste terrestre.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A Persian city famed for its turquoise and carpets. The Polos give up the sea route for the overland trail."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Balkh": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Balkh"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "L'antique cité afghane, « mère des villes », ravagée par Gengis Khan mais toujours sur la route de l'est.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The ancient Afghan city, ‘mother of cities,’ ravaged by Genghis Khan but still on the road east."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Pamir": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The Pamirs"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Le « toit du monde ». Marco décrit un plateau si haut qu'aucun oiseau n'y vole et que le feu y brûle pâle.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The ‘roof of the world.’ Marco describes a plateau so high that no bird flies there and fire burns pale."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Oasis mythique au pied du Pamir, carrefour des routes vers l'Inde, la Perse et la Chine profonde.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A legendary oasis at the foot of the Pamirs, crossroads of routes to India, Persia, and deep into China."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Désert du Taklamakan": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Taklamakan Desert"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "La traversée du « désert où l'on entre mais d'où l'on ne sort pas ». Des voix fantômes égarent les caravanes, dit Marco.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Crossing the ‘desert you enter but never leave.’ Ghostly voices lead caravans astray, Marco says."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Les grottes aux mille bouddhas marquent l'entrée dans le monde chinois. Le Grand Khan n'est plus si loin.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The caves of the thousand Buddhas mark the entrance into the Chinese world. The Great Khan is no longer far."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Shangdu": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Shangdu"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Xanadu, la résidence d'été de Kubilaï Khan et son palais de plaisir devenu légendaire.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Xanadu, Kublai Khan's summer residence and his pleasure palace, since become legendary."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Pékin": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Beijing"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "La cour de Kubilaï Khan. Marco Polo y passa dix-sept ans comme gouverneur et émissaire du Grand Khan.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The court of Kublai Khan. Marco Polo spent seventeen years there as a governor and envoy of the Great Khan."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Hannibal — traversée des Alpes": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Hannibal — Crossing the Alps"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Carthagène → Italie — 218 av. J.-C.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Cartagena → Italy — 218 BC"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Carthagène (Nouvelle-Carthage)": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Cartagena (New Carthage)"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Départ de l'armée punique, éléphants en tête. Hannibal a juré une haine éternelle à Rome.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The Punic army sets off, elephants at the front. Hannibal has sworn eternal hatred of Rome."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Passage de l'Èbre": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Crossing the Ebro"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Dernier fleuve avant la Gaule. L'armée s'allège des troupes jugées les moins sûres avant de s'engager plus loin.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The last river before Gaul. The army sheds its least reliable troops before pressing on."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Pyrénées franchies": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Crossing the Pyrenees"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Le col du Perthus laisse les tribus ibères derrière. Devant, la Gaule tout entière reste à traverser.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The Col du Perthus leaves the Iberian tribes behind. Ahead, all of Gaul still remains to be crossed."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Gaule narbonnaise": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Narbonensian Gaul"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Marche à travers un territoire officiellement neutre, mais où chaque tribu croisée peut basculer dans un camp ou l'autre.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Marching through officially neutral territory, where any tribe encountered could turn either way."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Passage du Rhône": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Crossing the Rhône"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Les éléphants transbordés sur des radeaux, terrifiés par l'eau, face aux Volques massés sur l'autre rive.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The elephants, terrified of the water, ferried across on rafts, facing the Volcae massed on the far bank."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Contreforts alpins": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Alpine Foothills"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Les Allobroges harcèlent la colonne dans les défilés étroits. Les premiers chariots basculent dans le vide.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The Allobroges harass the column in the narrow passes. The first wagons tumble into the void."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Ascension du col": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Climbing the Pass"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Neige précoce, éboulements, la colonne s'étire sur des kilomètres. Le froid tue plus sûrement que les tribus locales.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Early snow, rockslides, the column stretches for miles. The cold kills more surely than the local tribes."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Sommet du col": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The Summit"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Hannibal montre à ses hommes épuisés la plaine du Pô en contrebas. L'Italie, enfin visible, redonne courage à l'armée.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Hannibal shows his exhausted men the plain of the Po below. Italy, at last visible, restores the army's courage."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Descente périlleuse": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The Perilous Descent"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Verglas et glissades sur un sentier à peine tracé. Plusieurs éléphants glissent et sont perdus dans la descente.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Ice and slips on a barely marked path. Several elephants slide and are lost on the way down."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Sortie des Alpes": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Leaving the Alps"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Le territoire des Taurins s'ouvre enfin. Après quinze jours de montagne, l'armée touche la plaine italienne.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The territory of the Taurini finally opens up. After fifteen days in the mountains, the army reaches the Italian plain."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Siège de Turin": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Siege of Turin"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Première victoire sur le sol italien. La cité prise sert de base de ravitaillement pour l'armée exsangue.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "First victory on Italian soil. The captured city serves as a supply base for the exhausted army."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Bataille de la Trébie": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Battle of the Trebia"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Première grande victoire face aux légions romaines. Rome découvre qu'un général vient de traverser l'infranchissable.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "First great victory against the Roman legions. Rome discovers that a general has just crossed the uncrossable."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "L'Odyssée — trajet réel": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The Odyssey — The Real Route"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Troie → Ithaque en ligne droite — 10 ans d'errance": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Troy → Ithaca in a straight line — 10 years of wandering"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "La guerre achevée, Ulysse prend la mer. Ithaque n'est qu'à quelques jours de navigation favorable.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The war over, Odysseus takes to the sea. Ithaca is only a few days' favorable sailing away."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Lotophages — Djerba": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Lotus-Eaters — Djerba"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Chez les mangeurs de lotus, souvent situés à Djerba. Trois marins goûtent le fruit de l'oubli et refusent de repartir.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Among the lotus-eaters, often placed on Djerba. Three sailors taste the fruit of forgetting and refuse to leave."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Cyclopes — Sicile": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Cyclopes — Sicily"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "L'île de Polyphème. Ulysse lui crève l'œil avec un pieu d'olivier et s'échappe sous le ventre d'une brebis.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The island of Polyphemus. Odysseus blinds him with a stake of olive wood and escapes clinging beneath a ram."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Éole — Îles Éoliennes": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Aeolus — Aeolian Islands"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Le dieu des vents enferme les vents contraires dans une outre. Ouverte par des marins jaloux, elle rejette la flotte au large.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The god of the winds locks the contrary winds in a bag. Opened by jealous sailors, it blows the fleet back out to sea."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Lestrygons": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Laestrygonians"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Les géants cannibales fracassent onze des douze navires à coups de rochers. Seul celui d'Ulysse en réchappe.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The cannibal giants smash eleven of the twelve ships with boulders. Only Odysseus's own ship escapes."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Circé — Monte Circeo": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Circe — Monte Circeo"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "La magicienne transforme les compagnons en pourceaux. Ulysse résiste grâce à l'herbe magique de Hermès, puis reste un an.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The sorceress turns the men into swine. Odysseus resists thanks to Hermes' magic herb, then stays a year."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Sirènes — Golfe de Sorrente": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Sirens — Gulf of Sorrento"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Ulysse se fait attacher au mât pour entendre le chant fatal sans y succomber. Les rameurs ont les oreilles bouchées de cire.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Odysseus has himself tied to the mast to hear the fatal song without succumbing. The rowers' ears are stopped with wax."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Charybde & Scylla — Détroit de Messine": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Charybdis & Scylla — Strait of Messina"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Entre le monstre aux six têtes et le tourbillon dévoreur de navires, six compagnons périssent.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Between the six-headed monster and the ship-devouring whirlpool, six companions perish."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Ogygie — Calypso": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Ogygia — Calypso"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "L'île de la nymphe qui le retient et lui offre l'immortalité. Il préfère Ithaque et repart sur un simple radeau.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The nymph's island, where she holds him and offers immortality. He chooses Ithaca instead and leaves on a simple raft."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Phéaciens — Corfou": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Phaeacians — Corfu"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Les marins de Schérie, souvent identifiée à Corfou, l'écoutent puis le déposent endormi sur sa terre natale.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The sailors of Scheria, often identified with Corfu, listen to his tale then set him down asleep on his native shore."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Ithaque": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Ithaca"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Retour après dix ans. Pénélope a résisté, Télémaque a grandi. Il reste les prétendants à éliminer à l'arc.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Return after ten years. Penelope has held firm, Telemachus has grown. Only the suitors remain to be dealt with by the bow."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "L'Odyssée — voyage complet estimé": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The Odyssey — Estimated Full Voyage"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Avec tous les détours d'Ulysse — mer Méditerranée": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "With all of Odysseus's detours — Mediterranean Sea"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Départ après dix ans de siège. La flotte d'Ulysse compte douze navires et leurs équipages au complet.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Departure after ten years of siege. Odysseus's fleet numbers twelve ships with their crews at full strength."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Cicones — Ismaros": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Cicones — Ismarus"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Le premier pillage après Troie tourne mal : les Cicones contre-attaquent et tuent soixante-douze hommes d'Ulysse.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The first raid after Troy goes wrong: the Cicones counterattack and kill seventy-two of Odysseus's men."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Pays des Lotophages": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Land of the Lotus-Eaters"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Trois compagnons mangent le fruit de l'oubli et ne veulent plus rentrer — il faut les traîner de force aux navires.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Three companions eat the fruit of forgetting and no longer want to leave — they must be dragged by force back to the ships."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Pays des Cyclopes": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Land of the Cyclopes"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "L'île de Polyphème. La perte de six hommes et de la faveur de Poséidon vont compliquer dix ans de retour.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The island of Polyphemus. The loss of six men and Poseidon's favor will complicate ten years of homecoming."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "L'île d'Éole": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The Island of Aeolus"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Le dieu des vents offre une outre contenant les vents contraires. Ouverte par les compagnons jaloux, elle renvoie tout le monde au départ.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The god of the winds offers a bag holding the contrary winds. Opened by jealous companions, it blows everyone back to the start."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Les géants cannibales coulent onze des douze navires. La flotte d'Ulysse est réduite à un seul vaisseau.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The cannibal giants sink eleven of the twelve ships. Odysseus's fleet is reduced to a single vessel."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Circé — Aiaié": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Circe — Aeaea"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "La magicienne de l'île d'Aiaié change l'équipage en pourceaux. Ulysse lui résiste et demeure un an à ses côtés.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The sorceress of the island of Aeaea turns the crew into swine. Odysseus resists her and stays by her side for a year."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Pays des Morts": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Land of the Dead"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Ulysse descend aux Enfers consulter le devin Tirésias. Il revoit Achille, Ajax et l'ombre de sa propre mère.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Odysseus descends into the underworld to consult the seer Tiresias. He sees Achilles, Ajax, and the shade of his own mother again."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Les Sirènes": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The Sirens"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Ulysse se fait lier au mât pour entendre le chant mortel. Les rameurs, oreilles emplies de cire, forcent le passage.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Odysseus has himself bound to the mast to hear the deadly song. The rowers, ears filled with wax, force their way through."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Scylla & Charybde": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Scylla & Charybdis"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Entre le monstre aux six gueules et le tourbillon qui engloutit les navires. Six compagnons sont happés d'un coup.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Between the six-mouthed monster and the whirlpool that swallows ships. Six companions are seized in an instant."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Île du Soleil — Thrinacie": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Island of the Sun — Thrinacia"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Malgré l'interdit, les compagnons affamés dévorent les bœufs sacrés d'Hélios. Zeus foudroie le navire ; seul Ulysse survit.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Despite the warning, the starving companions devour Helios's sacred cattle. Zeus strikes the ship with lightning; only Odysseus survives."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Sept ans captif sur l'île de la nymphe Calypso. Elle lui offre l'immortalité. Il refuse et choisit Ithaque.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Seven years held captive on the nymph Calypso's island. She offers him immortality. He refuses and chooses Ithaca."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Schérie — les Phéaciens": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Scheria — The Phaeacians"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Peuple ami des dieux, les Phéaciens l'écoutent raconter dix ans d'aventures puis le ramènent endormi à Ithaque.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A people beloved of the gods, the Phaeacians listen to ten years of adventures, then carry him home asleep to Ithaca."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "L'arrivée en secret, le vieux chien Argos qui reconnaît son maître, et la vengeance des prétendants à l'arc d'ivoire.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The secret arrival, the old dog Argos recognizing his master, and vengeance upon the suitors with the ivory bow."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "L'Iliade — siège de Troie": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The Iliad — Siege of Troy"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Mycènes → Troie — 10 ans de siège": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Mycenae → Troy — 10 years of siege"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Mycènes": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Mycenae"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Agamemnon rassemble les rois grecs. La flotte de mille navires se forme pour venger l'honneur de Ménélas.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Agamemnon gathers the Greek kings. A fleet of a thousand ships forms to avenge Menelaus's honor."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Aulis": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Aulis"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Le port du rassemblement. Pour obtenir des vents favorables, Agamemnon doit sacrifier sa propre fille, Iphigénie.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The gathering port. To secure favorable winds, Agamemnon must sacrifice his own daughter, Iphigenia."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Débarquement en Troade": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Landing at the Troad"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Après la traversée de l'Égée, les Grecs abordent devant Troie. Protésilas, premier à sauter à terre, est le premier à tomber.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "After crossing the Aegean, the Greeks land before Troy. Protesilaus, first ashore, is the first to fall."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "La colère d'Achille": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The Wrath of Achilles"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Agamemnon lui prend Briséis. Achille se retire sous sa tente et prive les Grecs de leur plus grand guerrier.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Agamemnon takes Briseis from him. Achilles withdraws to his tent, depriving the Greeks of their greatest warrior."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Mort de Patrocle": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Death of Patroclus"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Revêtu des armes d'Achille, Patrocle repousse les Troyens mais tombe sous les coups d'Hector. La douleur rappelle Achille au combat.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Wearing Achilles' armor, Patroclus drives back the Trojans but falls to Hector. The grief brings Achilles back to battle."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Achille tue Hector": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Achilles Kills Hector"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Le duel décisif sous les murs. Achille traîne le corps d'Hector autour de la cité avant de le rendre au vieux roi Priam.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The decisive duel beneath the walls. Achilles drags Hector's body around the city before returning it to old King Priam."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Le cheval de bois": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The Wooden Horse"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "La ruse d'Ulysse : un cheval de bois géant abandonné devant les portes, que les Troyens introduisent eux-mêmes dans la ville.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Odysseus's ruse: a giant wooden horse left before the gates, which the Trojans themselves bring into the city."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "La chute de Troie": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "The Fall of Troy"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Dans la nuit, les Grecs sortis du cheval ouvrent les portes. Troie, jugée inexpugnable, s'effondre dans les flammes.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "In the night, the Greeks emerge from the horse and open the gates. Troy, thought impregnable, collapses in flames."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Copié !": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Copied!"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Appuyez deux fois pour copier la citation": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Double-tap to copy the quote"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Citation copiée": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Quote copied"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Pensée du jour": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Thought of the Day"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Une nouvelle pensée t'attend aujourd'hui.": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A new thought is waiting for you today."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Fermer la pensée du jour": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Close thought of the day"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Afficher la pensée du jour": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Show thought of the day"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Une pensée s'affiche à la première ouverture du jour, avec un rappel à midi si l'app n'a pas encore été ouverte": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "A thought appears the first time you open the app each day, with a reminder at noon if you haven't opened it yet"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Forêt": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Forest"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Océan": {
      "localizations": {
        "en": {
          "stringUnit": {
            "state": "translated",
            "value": "Ocean"
          }
        }
      }
